aws:cloudwatch/otelEnrichment:OtelEnrich.description:
Manages AWS CloudWatch OTel enrichment. This is a singleton resource that enables OTel enrichment at the account level.

> **NOTE:** This resource requires the <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`aws.observabilityadmin.TelemetryEnrichment`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`aws.observabilityadmin.TelemetryEnrichment`" pulumi-lang-go="`observabilityadmin.TelemetryEnrichment`" pulumi-lang-python="`observabilityadmin.TelemetryEnrichment`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`aws.observabilityadmin.TelemetryEnrichment`" pulumi-lang-java="`aws.observabilityadmin.TelemetryEnrichment`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`aws_observabilityadmin_telemetry_enrichment`">`aws.observabilityadmin.TelemetryEnrichment`</span> resource to be configured first. Without telemetry enrichment enabled, OTel enrichment will not function properly even if the API accepts the configuration.

> **NOTE:** Creating this Terraform resource starts AWS CloudWatch OTel enrichment and deleting this Terraform resource stops AWS CloudWatch OTel enrichment.

Filters are evaluated as follows. <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`includeFilter`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`IncludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-go="`includeFilter`" pulumi-lang-python="`include_filter`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`includeFilter`" pulumi-lang-java="`includeFilter`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`include_filter`">`includeFilter`</span> is applied first, then the <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`excludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`ExcludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-go="`excludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-python="`exclude_filter`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`excludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-java="`excludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`exclude_filter`">`excludeFilter`</span> match set is subtracted from the result. Exclusion always wins, so a metric matched by both is not enriched. An inactive direction is permissive: with no <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`includeFilter`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`IncludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-go="`includeFilter`" pulumi-lang-python="`include_filter`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`includeFilter`" pulumi-lang-java="`includeFilter`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`include_filter`">`includeFilter`</span>, every supported namespace is in scope, and with no <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`excludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`ExcludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-go="`excludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-python="`exclude_filter`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`excludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-java="`excludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`exclude_filter`">`excludeFilter`</span>, nothing is removed. Namespaces and metric names are matched exactly and case-sensitively, with no wildcards or prefixes, so `AWS/EC2` matches only `AWS/EC2`. At most 100 selectors are allowed across <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`includeFilter`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`IncludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-go="`includeFilter`" pulumi-lang-python="`include_filter`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`includeFilter`" pulumi-lang-java="`includeFilter`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`include_filter`">`includeFilter`</span> and <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`excludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`ExcludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-go="`excludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-python="`exclude_filter`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`excludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-java="`excludeFilter`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`exclude_filter`">`excludeFilter`</span> **combined**. Two lists of 60 selectors each satisfy the per-list limit but are rejected together.

