aws:observabilityadmin/telemetryRule:Tel.description:
Manages an AWS CloudWatch Observability Admin Telemetry Rule.

A telemetry rule defines how telemetry data (logs, metrics, or traces) should be collected for AWS resources within an AWS account. The rule can target one or more Regions and optionally configure a destination (such as CloudWatch Logs or S3) along with source-specific parameters for VPC flow logs, WAF logs, CloudTrail events, ELB access logs, and more.

> **NOTE:** Before using this resource, telemetry evaluation must be enabled for your AWS account. Use the <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`aws.observabilityadmin.TelemetryEvaluation`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`aws.observabilityadmin.TelemetryEvaluation`" pulumi-lang-go="`observabilityadmin.TelemetryEvaluation`" pulumi-lang-python="`observabilityadmin.TelemetryEvaluation`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`aws.observabilityadmin.TelemetryEvaluation`" pulumi-lang-java="`aws.observabilityadmin.TelemetryEvaluation`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`aws_observabilityadmin_telemetry_evaluation`">`aws.observabilityadmin.TelemetryEvaluation`</span> resource to enable it.

