### Read Existing Notifications and Re-emit Them

The S3 [`PutBucketNotificationConfiguration`](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_PutBucketNotificationConfiguration.html) API replaces the entire notification configuration on every call, so a single <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`aws.s3.BucketNotification`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`aws.s3.BucketNotification`" pulumi-lang-go="`s3.BucketNotification`" pulumi-lang-python="`s3.BucketNotification`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`aws.s3.BucketNotification`" pulumi-lang-java="`aws.s3.BucketNotification`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`aws_s3_bucket_notification`">`aws.s3.BucketNotification`</span> resource owns the bucket. To preserve notifications already on the bucket — or to mirror one bucket's configuration onto another — read them with this data source and pass them through <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`dynamic`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Dynamic`" pulumi-lang-go="`dynamic`" pulumi-lang-python="`dynamic`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`dynamic`" pulumi-lang-java="`dynamic`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`dynamic`">`dynamic`</span> blocks. The data source's output shape matches the resource's input shape, so each block forwards directly.

<!--Start PulumiCodeChooser -->
